# Gradio application rules

This directory is the user-owned application area.

- Keep `main.py` as the container entry point unless Docker, CI and root guidance change together.
- Keep Serve port 7860 and external binding through `GRADIO_SERVER_NAME=0.0.0.0`.
- Do not add `auth=` or another application-level login/user system.
- Keep `share=False`; SciLifeLab Serve provides the hosted URL.
- Uploaded/temp files should be ephemeral unless intentionally written to an approved Serve storage mount path.
- Do not persist sensitive/personal/user data.
- Keep runtime dependencies in `requirements.txt`; starter policy uses exact `==` pins.
- The current Serve Gradio guide reports a known deployment issue with Private/Project permissions; deployment guidance uses Link/Public.

Reference: https://serve.scilifelab.se/docs/application-hosting/gradio/
